<!--
  Discord's mark, for the row on the developer screen that opens an invite to the developer's server.

  A brand mark rather than a stand-in from the Material set, which has none: a generic
  glyph beside "Discord" would name a category, not say where the row goes. Drawn as a
  single-colour silhouette and tinted by the caller, the way ic_launcher_monochrome and
  the ic_stat_* icons are.

  The arcs arrive from the source with their large-arc and sweep flags run together as
  `00`, which Android's generic float scanner reads as one number and leaves the arc a
  parameter short; the two digits are separated here and nothing else is changed.

  Long for a vector path, and lint says so. The check is about paths whose parsing and
  allocation cost shows up during layout or animation; this one is parsed once, for a
  20 dp glyph, on a screen reached from the bottom of Settings. Shortening it would mean
  either reprecising — the mark is mostly relative segments, so an error in one is
  carried by every one after it — or redrawing someone's trademark.

  Path from the simple-icons set (CC0). The mark is Discord's own.
-->
